2026-07-24T13:36:10.7406074Z             "body": "## Summary\nThis PR enhances the web UI with better messaging and navigation, improves the config history system to handle legacy data formats, and refines several UI elements for better usability.\n\n## Key Changes\n\n### UI/UX Improvements\n- **Toast message system**: Replaced inline error messages with fixed-position toast notifications that don't cause layout shifts. Added manual dismiss buttons and differentiated auto-dismiss behavior (success messages auto-clear after 4s; warnings/errors persist until dismissed).\n- **Floating scroll navigation**: Added fixed scroll-to-top and scroll-to-bottom buttons in the bottom-right corner for easier navigation on the long config page, with responsive positioning on mobile.\n- **Collapsible sections**: Converted the \"Per-domain DKIM selectors\" panel to a collapsible `<details>` element with a dynamic hint showing the count of configured domains.\n- **External link indicators**: Added subtle \"↗\" icons to external links (API docs) across all pages with proper accessibility attributes.\n- **Navigation labels**: Renamed \"Tokens\" to \"Access Tokens\" for clarity across all pages.\n\n### Config History Migration\n- **Legacy format support**: Added backward compatibility for pre-split config history files where revision bodies were embedded inline in `config-history.json`. The system now:\n  - Reads legacy inline bodies on load\n  - Automatically externalizes them to individual `config-rev-{id}.json` files\n  - Collapses the index to the body-less format after successful migration\n  - Ensures `GetRevision()` can find all revisions regardless of storage format\n- **Robust migration**: Uses best-effort approach with retry logic; skips collapsing the index if any body fails to externalize, preventing data loss.\n\n### Implementation Details\n- Toast messages use CSS animations (`msgIn` keyframe) for smooth entrance and are positioned with `position: fixed` to prevent reflow.\n- Scroll navigation buttons are circular with hover effects and use `aria-hidden=\"true\"` since they're supplementary controls.\n- History migration normalizes domain lists and DKIM selectors during externalization to maintain data consistency.\n- Added comprehensive test coverage for legacy history migration with verification that both old and new formats work correctly.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015QvoXY3GYdRayQzh6a6JPv",
